	"description": "Who ate my context window? A true-crime parody: four rumoured suspects (drawn, folklore, not data), then the real harness map on the demo project: Instructions 324 tokens, a rule that matches no file, and Skills as most of what loads before the first prompt (2.4k of 2.8k). The lint is rule-based, no LLM. Demo project (Harbor Goods). Real captures of Insilode, a code editor built on VS Code. Voice: synthetic (AI-generated). Music composed in code. Free and open source: insilode.dev",
